# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is never committed.

# Vision model for reading logbook photos (Google AI Studio key).
# Without it the app still runs: sample pages show their stored reading and
# photo upload says it is not configured.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: comma-separated models to try in order. The route moves to the
# next one when a model is overloaded, out of quota, or breaks off mid-answer.
# Default: gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# On the free tier each model has its own small daily request allowance (the
# API's error on 4 Oct 2026 reported "limit: 20" for gemini-3.5-flash), so
# keep more than one model in the list.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash,gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Optional: minimal | low | medium | high. Default low; higher is slower and
# did not read the sample pages any better. With minimal or low, a model that
# has written nothing after 25 s is given up on and the next one is asked.
# With medium or high the route waits 45 s for the first word, which leaves
# time for one model only inside the 55 s it has for a page, so a slow page
# fails with "took too long" instead of falling through the list.
# GEMINI_THINKING=low

# Optional: how many model calls this server instance may make in any 24
# hours, across all visitors (default 40) and for one visitor (default 10).
# A page normally takes one call; opening the same photo again within six
# hours takes none. The defaults fit a free key shared by several visitors;
# raise both with a paid key. The counts are kept in memory, so they start
# again when the server restarts, and each instance on a serverless host
# keeps its own. A browser on the server's own machine (localhost) is held
# only to the first number.
# EXTRACT_DAILY_LIMIT=40
# EXTRACT_DAILY_PER_CALLER=10

# Optional: extra public host names (comma-separated, no scheme) the page may
# be served from. Only needed behind a proxy or tunnel that rewrites the Host
# header without setting X-Forwarded-Host; otherwise the route's same-site
# check works unaided.
# EXTRACT_ALLOWED_HOSTS=jallog.example.com
